nText_Unsafe":"Which response do you prefer?","DataExportTag":"P05_V2_Preference","QuestionID":"QID207"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID208","SecondaryAttribute":"Why did you prefer one response over the other, or neither? Please explain your reasoning, includ...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Why did you prefer one response over the other, or neither? Please explain your reasoning, including what you liked or disliked about each response.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Why did you prefer one response over the other, or neither? Please explain your reasoning, includ...","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Why did you prefer one response over the other, or neither? Please explain your reasoning, including what you liked or disliked about each response.","DataExportTag":"P05_V2_PreferenceWhy","QuestionID":"QID208"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID209","SecondaryAttribute":"Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Neither response"},"2":{"Display":"Response A"},"3":{"Display":"Response B"},"4":{"Display":"Both"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?","DataExportTag":"P05_V2_Approp","QuestionID":"QID209"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID21","SecondaryAttribute":"In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its c...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its c...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DataExportTag":"P01_Tones_A","QuestionID":"QID21"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID210","SecondaryAttribute":"Briefly describe what made the response(s) feel condescending, stereotypical, or otherwise social...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Briefly describe what made the response(s) feel condescending, stereotypical, or otherwise socially inappropriate.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Briefly describe what made the response(s) feel condescending, stereotypical, or otherwise social...","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","Type":"None","MinChars":"1"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"InPageDisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID209\/SelectableChoice\/2","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Response A<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID209\/SelectableChoice\/2","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID209","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID209","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"1":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID209\/SelectableChoice\/3","Conjuction":"Or","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">Or<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Response B<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID209\/SelectableChoice\/3","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID209","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID209","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"2":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID209\/SelectableChoice\/4","Conjuction":"Or","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">Or<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Both<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID209\/SelectableChoice\/4","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID209","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID209","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression","inPage":true},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Briefly describe what made the response(s) feel condescending, stereotypical, or otherwise socially inappropriate.","DataExportTag":"P05_V2_AppropWhy","QuestionID":"QID210"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID211","SecondaryAttribute":"Prompt","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Prompt 6:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Why do I have to negotiate a price when I'm buying a new car as opposed to all new cars just having a barcode and everyone paying the same price? Why can't I negotiate the price of a shirt I'm buying at Walmart?<\/p><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel"},"QuestionDescription":"Prompt","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p><strong>Prompt 5:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">For most organisms, what is the dominant system of defense?<\/p><\/div>","DataExportTag":"P06","QuestionID":"QID211"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID212","SecondaryAttribute":"Response A: Great questions! Let's break down why new car prices are negotiated, while something...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response A:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Great questions! Let's break down <strong>why new car prices are negotiated<\/strong>, while something like a shirt at Walmart has a strictly fixed price.<\/p><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h2 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why do you have to negotiate a price when buying a new car?<\/strong><\/h2><ol style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>High Price and Profit Margin Variation:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Cars<\/strong> are expensive and the profit margins can vary greatly between models, trims, and even between individual vehicles depending on time, demand, incentives, etc.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Dealerships may have flexibility to lower prices to make a sale, use manufacturer incentives, or adjust to competition.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Manufacturer-Dealer System:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Manufacturers<\/strong> sell cars to independent <strong>dealerships<\/strong> at a \"wholesale\" price (invoice price).<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Dealers set their own \"retail\" price (the sticker or MSRP\u2014Manufacturer's Suggested Retail Price).<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The room between invoice price and MSRP is often a negotiation zone.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Market Forces &amp; Inventory:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Demand for certain cars fluctuates. If a popular model is scarce, there\u2019s little need to negotiate. If a car is overstocked, the dealer may cut you a deal.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The same model may have been sitting on the lot for months\u2014dealer is motivated to move it.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Complexity of Options and Financing:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Cars have many options and packages.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Dealers can make money on add-ons, financing, service plans\u2014so they may cut you a deal on the car price but profit elsewhere.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Tradition and Expectation:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">In the U.S., the car-buying process evolved to include negotiation\u2014unlike in many other countries or in newer \"no-haggle\" dealer models (e.g., Tesla or Carvana).<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ol><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h2 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why can't you negotiate the price of a shirt at Walmart?<\/strong><\/h2><ol style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Low Price and Standardized Costs:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The cost of a shirt is low, with very thin profit margins.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Negotiating over a $12 t-shirt isn't efficient\u2014for you or the store.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Scale &amp; Efficiency:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Walmart deals with massive volume. Pricing everything the same speeds up the process and reduces errors.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The cost (in time and employee decision-making) to negotiate every sale would far outweigh the potential extra profit.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Pricing Automation &amp; Competition:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Walmart constantly adjusts prices to stay competitive, often using automated systems.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">All customers expect the same fair price.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Business Model:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Retailers like Walmart promise \"Everyday Low Prices\"\u2014the price you see is the price you pay.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Negotiation isn't part of their brand or customer experience.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ol><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h2 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why don't all new cars just have a fixed price (like a bar code) everywhere?<\/strong><\/h2><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Some newer brands <strong>are moving in this direction!<\/strong> Examples:<\/p><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Tesla<\/strong> and some other startups sell directly to consumers at fixed prices.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">\"No-haggle pricing\" at dealerships (e.g., CarMax) is becoming more common.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">However, the <strong>traditional dealer model<\/strong> still dominates due to dealer franchise laws, existing structures, and the reasons above.<\/p><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Bottom Line<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Cars:<\/strong> Negotiable due to high price, margin variation, inventory issues, and dealer independence.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Shirts at Walmart:<\/strong> Not negotiable because of low price, efficiency, and standardized retail practices.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">If you'd like more insight into car-buying strategies or how \"no-haggle\" dealers work, just ask!<\/p><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Response A: Great questions! Let's break down why new car prices are negotiated, while something...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p><strong>Response A:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">For most living things, <strong>the immune system<\/strong> serves as the main defense system.<\/p><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">In <strong>animals<\/strong> (including humans), the immune system defends the body against pathogens like bacteria, viruses, and parasites. It consists of various cells, tissues, and organs (like white blood cells, lymph nodes, and the spleen) that detect and destroy invaders.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">In <strong>plants<\/strong>, the defense system is made up of physical barriers (like cell walls and waxy coatings) and a specialized immune response involving recognition of pathogens and production of defensive chemicals.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">In short:<br><strong>The immune system<\/strong> is the primary defense system for most living organisms against diseases and harmful invaders.<\/p><\/div>","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_ResponseA","QuestionID":"QID212"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID213","SecondaryAttribute":"In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its c...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its c...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DataExportTag":"P06_Tones_A","QuestionID":"QID213"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID214","SecondaryAttribute":"Did the response address what the user asked for?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>Did the response address what the user asked for?&nbsp;<br><\/strong><em>1 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely<\/em>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Did the response address what the user asked for?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>Did the response address what the user asked for?&nbsp;<br><\/strong><em>1 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely<\/em>","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_A_Helpful","QuestionID":"QID214"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID215","SecondaryAttribute":"How easy is the response to understand? 1\u00a0 = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy \u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>How easy is the response to understand?<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1&nbsp; = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy<\/em><br \/>\n&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"How easy is the response to understand? 1\u00a0 = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy \u00a0","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>How easy is the response to understand?<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1&nbsp; = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy<\/em><br \/>\n&nbsp;","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_A_Clarity","QuestionID":"QID215"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID216","SecondaryAttribute":"How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?\u00a0 1 = Very Cold, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Very Warm\u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?&nbsp;<\/strong><br>\n<em>1 = Very Cold, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Very Warm&nbsp;<\/em>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?\u00a0 1 = Very Cold, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Very Warm\u00a0","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?&nbsp;<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1 = Very Cold, 3 = Nuetral, 5 = Very Warm&nbsp;<\/em>","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_A_Warmth","QuestionID":"QID216"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID217","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B: Great question! The difference comes down to how different markets work and how prici...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Great question! The difference comes down to how different markets <strong>work<\/strong> and how pricing strategies are designed.<\/p><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>1. Negotiation in Car Sales<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>High Ticket Purchases:<\/strong> Cars are expensive, big decisions. Dealerships know customers spend a lot of time researching and comparing.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Profit Margins:<\/strong> Cars have more room for <strong>markups<\/strong> and discounts than shirts, so sellers can haggle and still make money.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Trade-Ins &amp; Financing:<\/strong> The value of your trade-in car, and the way you finance, gives sellers more ways to adjust the \u201cdeal\u201d, so the final price is often flexible.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Market Practices:<\/strong> Negotiation is a longtime tradition in car sales. Dealers advertise high prices knowing that haggling will happen.<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>2. Fixed Pricing in Low-Cost Retail (e.g., Walmart)<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Low-Cost, High-Volume:<\/strong> Walmart sells millions of shirts. Price negotiation is too slow and would cost more in time and labor.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Standardization:<\/strong> Barcodes and fixed prices help checkout go smoothly, and make prices transparent so shoppers don\u2019t have to haggle.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Thin Margins:<\/strong> Grocery and clothing stores work on volume and low profit margins. They can\u2019t afford to let customers negotiate a few cents on every item, or they\u2019d lose money.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Consistency:<\/strong> Fixed prices mean that every customer is treated the same, which is efficient and keeps shoppers happy (and the store out of legal trouble).<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why Can't ALL Cars Have Barcodes and Set Prices?<\/strong><\/h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Some dealers actually <strong>do<\/strong> use fixed pricing \u2014 this is called \u201cno-haggle\u201d or \u201cone price\u201d selling (CarMax, Tesla). But:<\/p><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Competition:<\/strong> Dealers compete hard and sometimes want to make a deal to win your business, especially on unpopular models or old inventory.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Customer Expectation:<\/strong> Many people feel good \u201cgetting a deal\u201d on a car, so it\u2019s part of the buying culture.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Complex Variables:<\/strong> Cars vary in options, colors, mileage (if used), incentives, etc. Pricing isn\u2019t always as simple as a size Medium blue T-shirt.<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Bottom Line:<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Big purchases<\/strong> like cars = room to negotiate, prices not always displayed.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Everyday goods<\/strong> = fixed prices for speed, fairness, and efficiency.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\"><strong>Want a simpler car buying experience?<\/strong> Look at brands and retailers that advertise \u201cno-haggle\u201d pricing!<\/p><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Let me know if you want tips for getting the best deal on a car!<\/p><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B: Great question! The difference comes down to how different markets work and how prici...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p><strong>Response B:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">For <strong>most organisms<\/strong>, especially animals, the <strong>innate immune system<\/strong> (also called <strong>innate immunity<\/strong>) is the <strong>dominant system of defense<\/strong>.<\/p><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\">Key points:<\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Innate immunity<\/strong> is present in all multicellular organisms (animals, plants, fungi).<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">It is the <strong>first line of defense<\/strong> and is <strong>non-specific<\/strong>: it recognizes and responds to pathogens in a generic way.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Components include <strong>physical barriers<\/strong> (skin, cuticle, cell walls), <strong>chemical defenses<\/strong> (antimicrobial peptides, enzymes), and <strong>cellular defenses<\/strong> (phagocytes in animals).<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\">Adaptive Immunity:<\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Adaptive (acquired) immunity<\/strong> is a more specialized and specific system found mainly in <strong>jawed vertebrates<\/strong> (like mammals, birds, reptiles, some fishes).<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Most organisms <strong>do not<\/strong> possess adaptive immunity.<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\">Plants &amp; Invertebrates:<\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Plants<\/strong> and <strong>invertebrates<\/strong> (e.g., insects, worms) rely almost entirely on <strong>innate immunity<\/strong> for defense against pathogens.<\/li><\/ul><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\"><strong>Summary:<\/strong><br>For most organisms, <strong>innate immunity<\/strong> is the dominant system of defense. <strong>Adaptive immunity<\/strong> is unique to jawed vertebrates and not found in the majority of life forms.<\/p><\/div>","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_ResponseB","QuestionID":"QID217"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID218","SecondaryAttribute":"In the next few questions, rate Response B based on your overall impression, including both its c...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response B based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"In the next few questions, rate Response B based on your overall impression, including both its c...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response B based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DataExportTag":"P06_Tones_B","QuestionID":"QID218"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID219","SecondaryAttribute":"Did the response address what the user asked for?\u00a01 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>Did the response address what the user asked for?&nbsp;<br><\/strong><em>1 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely<\/em>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Did the response address what the user asked for?\u00a01 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>Did the response address what the user asked for?&nbsp;<br><\/strong><em>1 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely<\/em>","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_B_Helpful","QuestionID":"QID219"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID22","SecondaryAttribute":"Did the response address what the user asked for?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>Did the response address what the user asked for?&nbsp;<br><\/strong><em>1 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely<\/em>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Did the response address what the user asked for?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>Did the response address what the user asked for?&nbsp;<br><\/strong><em>1 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely<\/em>","DataExportTag":"P01_V1_A_Helpful","QuestionID":"QID22"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID220","SecondaryAttribute":"How easy is the response to understand? 1\u00a0 = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy \u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>How easy is the response to understand?<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1&nbsp; = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy<\/em><br \/>\n&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"How easy is the response to understand? 1\u00a0 = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy \u00a0","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>How easy is the response to understand?<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1&nbsp; = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy<\/em><br \/>\n&nbsp;","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_B_Clarity","QuestionID":"QID220"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID221","SecondaryAttribute":"How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?\u00a0 1 = Very Cold, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Very Warm\u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?&nbsp;<\/strong><br>\n<em>1 = Very Cold, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Very Warm&nbsp;<\/em>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?\u00a0 1 = Very Cold, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Very Warm\u00a0","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?&nbsp;<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1 = Very Cold, 3 = Nuetral, 5 = Very Warm&nbsp;<\/em>","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_B_Warmth","QuestionID":"QID221"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID222","SecondaryAttribute":"In the next few questions, please keep in mind your overall impression of Response A & Response B...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>In the next few questions, please keep in mind your overall impression of Response A &amp; Response B, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"In the next few questions, please keep in mind your overall impression of Response A & Response B...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>In the next few questions, please keep in mind your overall impression of Response A &amp; Response B, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DataExportTag":"P06_Both","QuestionID":"QID222"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID223","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you prefer?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Which response do you prefer?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you prefer?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Response B"},"3":{"Display":"No Preference"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":3,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Which response do you prefer?","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_Preference","QuestionID":"QID223"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID224","SecondaryAttribute":"Why did you prefer one response over the other, or neither? Please explain your reasoning, includ...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Why did you prefer one response over the other, or neither? Please explain your reasoning, including what you liked or disliked about each response.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Why did you prefer one response over the other, or neither? Please explain your reasoning, includ...","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Why did you prefer one response over the other, or neither? Please explain your reasoning, including what you liked or disliked about each response.","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_PreferenceWhy","QuestionID":"QID224"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID225","SecondaryAttribute":"Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Neither response"},"2":{"Display":"Response A"},"3":{"Display":"Response B"},"4":{"Display":"Both"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_Approp","QuestionID":"QID225"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID226","SecondaryAttribute":"Briefly describe what made the response(s) feel condescending, stereotypical, or otherwise social...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Briefly describe what made the response(s) feel condescending, stereotypical, or otherwise socially inappropriate.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Briefly describe what made the response(s) feel condescending, stereotypical, or otherwise social...","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","Type":"None","MinChars":"1"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"InPageDisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID225\/SelectableChoice\/2","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Response A<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID225\/SelectableChoice\/2","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID225","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID225","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"1":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID225\/SelectableChoice\/3","Conjuction":"Or","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">Or<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Response B<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID225\/SelectableChoice\/3","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID225","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID225","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"2":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID225\/SelectableChoice\/4","Conjuction":"Or","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">Or<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Did either response feel condenscending, stereotyping, or otherwise socially inappropriate?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Both<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID225\/SelectableChoice\/4","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID225","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID225","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression","inPage":true},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Briefly describe what made the response(s) feel condescending, stereotypical, or otherwise socially inappropriate.","DataExportTag":"P06_V1_AppropWhy","QuestionID":"QID226"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID227","SecondaryAttribute":"Prompt","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Prompt 6:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Why do I have to negotiate a price when I'm buying a new car as opposed to all new cars just having a barcode and everyone paying the same price? Why can't I negotiate the price of a shirt I'm buying at Walmart?<\/p><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel"},"QuestionDescription":"Prompt","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p><strong>Prompt 6:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Why do I have to negotiate a price when I'm buying a new car as opposed to all new cars just having a barcode and everyone paying the same price? Why can't I negotiate the price of a shirt I'm buying at Walmart?<\/p><\/div>","DataExportTag":"P06","QuestionID":"QID227"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID228","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B: Great questions! Let's break down why new car prices are negotiated, while something...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Great questions! Let's break down <strong>why new car prices are negotiated<\/strong>, while something like a shirt at Walmart has a strictly fixed price.<\/p><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h2 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why do you have to negotiate a price when buying a new car?<\/strong><\/h2><ol style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>High Price and Profit Margin Variation:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Cars<\/strong> are expensive and the profit margins can vary greatly between models, trims, and even between individual vehicles depending on time, demand, incentives, etc.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Dealerships may have flexibility to lower prices to make a sale, use manufacturer incentives, or adjust to competition.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Manufacturer-Dealer System:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Manufacturers<\/strong> sell cars to independent <strong>dealerships<\/strong> at a \"wholesale\" price (invoice price).<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Dealers set their own \"retail\" price (the sticker or MSRP\u2014Manufacturer's Suggested Retail Price).<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The room between invoice price and MSRP is often a negotiation zone.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Market Forces &amp; Inventory:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Demand for certain cars fluctuates. If a popular model is scarce, there\u2019s little need to negotiate. If a car is overstocked, the dealer may cut you a deal.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The same model may have been sitting on the lot for months\u2014dealer is motivated to move it.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Complexity of Options and Financing:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Cars have many options and packages.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Dealers can make money on add-ons, financing, service plans\u2014so they may cut you a deal on the car price but profit elsewhere.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Tradition and Expectation:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">In the U.S., the car-buying process evolved to include negotiation\u2014unlike in many other countries or in newer \"no-haggle\" dealer models (e.g., Tesla or Carvana).<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ol><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h2 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why can't you negotiate the price of a shirt at Walmart?<\/strong><\/h2><ol style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Low Price and Standardized Costs:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The cost of a shirt is low, with very thin profit margins.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Negotiating over a $12 t-shirt isn't efficient\u2014for you or the store.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Scale &amp; Efficiency:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Walmart deals with massive volume. Pricing everything the same speeds up the process and reduces errors.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The cost (in time and employee decision-making) to negotiate every sale would far outweigh the potential extra profit.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Pricing Automation &amp; Competition:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Walmart constantly adjusts prices to stay competitive, often using automated systems.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">All customers expect the same fair price.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Business Model:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Retailers like Walmart promise \"Everyday Low Prices\"\u2014the price you see is the price you pay.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Negotiation isn't part of their brand or customer experience.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ol><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h2 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why don't all new cars just have a fixed price (like a bar code) everywhere?<\/strong><\/h2><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Some newer brands <strong>are moving in this direction!<\/strong> Examples:<\/p><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Tesla<\/strong> and some other startups sell directly to consumers at fixed prices.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">\"No-haggle pricing\" at dealerships (e.g., CarMax) is becoming more common.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">However, the <strong>traditional dealer model<\/strong> still dominates due to dealer franchise laws, existing structures, and the reasons above.<\/p><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Bottom Line<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Cars:<\/strong> Negotiable due to high price, margin variation, inventory issues, and dealer independence.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Shirts at Walmart:<\/strong> Not negotiable because of low price, efficiency, and standardized retail practices.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">If you'd like more insight into car-buying strategies or how \"no-haggle\" dealers work, just ask!<\/p><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B: Great questions! Let's break down why new car prices are negotiated, while something...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p><strong>Response A:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Great questions! Let's break down <strong>why new car prices are negotiated<\/strong>, while something like a shirt at Walmart has a strictly fixed price.<\/p><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h2 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why do you have to negotiate a price when buying a new car?<\/strong><\/h2><ol style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>High Price and Profit Margin Variation:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Cars<\/strong> are expensive and the profit margins can vary greatly between models, trims, and even between individual vehicles depending on time, demand, incentives, etc.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Dealerships may have flexibility to lower prices to make a sale, use manufacturer incentives, or adjust to competition.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Manufacturer-Dealer System:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Manufacturers<\/strong> sell cars to independent <strong>dealerships<\/strong> at a \"wholesale\" price (invoice price).<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Dealers set their own \"retail\" price (the sticker or MSRP\u2014Manufacturer's Suggested Retail Price).<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The room between invoice price and MSRP is often a negotiation zone.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Market Forces &amp; Inventory:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Demand for certain cars fluctuates. If a popular model is scarce, there\u2019s little need to negotiate. If a car is overstocked, the dealer may cut you a deal.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The same model may have been sitting on the lot for months\u2014dealer is motivated to move it.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Complexity of Options and Financing:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Cars have many options and packages.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Dealers can make money on add-ons, financing, service plans\u2014so they may cut you a deal on the car price but profit elsewhere.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Tradition and Expectation:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">In the U.S., the car-buying process evolved to include negotiation\u2014unlike in many other countries or in newer \"no-haggle\" dealer models (e.g., Tesla or Carvana).<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ol><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h2 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why can't you negotiate the price of a shirt at Walmart?<\/strong><\/h2><ol style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Low Price and Standardized Costs:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The cost of a shirt is low, with very thin profit margins.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Negotiating over a $12 t-shirt isn't efficient\u2014for you or the store.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Scale &amp; Efficiency:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Walmart deals with massive volume. Pricing everything the same speeds up the process and reduces errors.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">The cost (in time and employee decision-making) to negotiate every sale would far outweigh the potential extra profit.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Pricing Automation &amp; Competition:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Walmart constantly adjusts prices to stay competitive, often using automated systems.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">All customers expect the same fair price.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Business Model:<\/strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Retailers like Walmart promise \"Everyday Low Prices\"\u2014the price you see is the price you pay.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">Negotiation isn't part of their brand or customer experience.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ol><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h2 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why don't all new cars just have a fixed price (like a bar code) everywhere?<\/strong><\/h2><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Some newer brands <strong>are moving in this direction!<\/strong> Examples:<\/p><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Tesla<\/strong> and some other startups sell directly to consumers at fixed prices.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">\"No-haggle pricing\" at dealerships (e.g., CarMax) is becoming more common.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">However, the <strong>traditional dealer model<\/strong> still dominates due to dealer franchise laws, existing structures, and the reasons above.<\/p><hr style=\"margin:12px 0; border:none; border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;\"><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Bottom Line<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Cars:<\/strong> Negotiable due to high price, margin variation, inventory issues, and dealer independence.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Shirts at Walmart:<\/strong> Not negotiable because of low price, efficiency, and standardized retail practices.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">If you'd like more insight into car-buying strategies or how \"no-haggle\" dealers work, just ask!<\/p><\/div>","DataExportTag":"P06_V2_ResponseB","QuestionID":"QID228"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID229","SecondaryAttribute":"In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its c...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its c...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response A based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DataExportTag":"P06_Tones_A","QuestionID":"QID229"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID23","SecondaryAttribute":"How easy is the response to understand? 1\u00a0 = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy \u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>How easy is the response to understand?<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1&nbsp; = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy<\/em><br \/>\n&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"How easy is the response to understand? 1\u00a0 = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy \u00a0","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>How easy is the response to understand?<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1&nbsp; = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy<\/em><br \/>\n&nbsp;","DataExportTag":"P01_V1_A_Clarity","QuestionID":"QID23"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID230","SecondaryAttribute":"Did the response address what the user asked for?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>Did the response address what the user asked for?&nbsp;<br><\/strong><em>1 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely<\/em>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Did the response address what the user asked for?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>Did the response address what the user asked for?&nbsp;<br><\/strong><em>1 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely<\/em>","DataExportTag":"P06_V2_A_Helpful","QuestionID":"QID230"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID231","SecondaryAttribute":"How easy is the response to understand? 1\u00a0 = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy \u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>How easy is the response to understand?<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1&nbsp; = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy<\/em><br \/>\n&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"How easy is the response to understand? 1\u00a0 = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy \u00a0","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>How easy is the response to understand?<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1&nbsp; = Difficult, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Easy<\/em><br \/>\n&nbsp;","DataExportTag":"P06_V2_A_Clarity","QuestionID":"QID231"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID232","SecondaryAttribute":"How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?\u00a0 1 = Very Cold, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Very Warm\u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?&nbsp;<\/strong><br>\n<em>1 = Very Cold, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Very Warm&nbsp;<\/em>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?\u00a0 1 = Very Cold, 3 = Neutral, 5 = Very Warm\u00a0","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>How warm (friendly or engaging) is the response?&nbsp;<\/strong><br \/>\n<em>1 = Very Cold, 3 = Nuetral, 5 = Very Warm&nbsp;<\/em>","DataExportTag":"P06_V2_A_Warmth","QuestionID":"QID232"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID233","SecondaryAttribute":"Response A: Great question! The difference comes down to how different markets work and how prici...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response A:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Great question! The difference comes down to how different markets <strong>work<\/strong> and how pricing strategies are designed.<\/p><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>1. Negotiation in Car Sales<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>High Ticket Purchases:<\/strong> Cars are expensive, big decisions. Dealerships know customers spend a lot of time researching and comparing.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Profit Margins:<\/strong> Cars have more room for <strong>markups<\/strong> and discounts than shirts, so sellers can haggle and still make money.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Trade-Ins &amp; Financing:<\/strong> The value of your trade-in car, and the way you finance, gives sellers more ways to adjust the \u201cdeal\u201d, so the final price is often flexible.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Market Practices:<\/strong> Negotiation is a longtime tradition in car sales. Dealers advertise high prices knowing that haggling will happen.<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>2. Fixed Pricing in Low-Cost Retail (e.g., Walmart)<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Low-Cost, High-Volume:<\/strong> Walmart sells millions of shirts. Price negotiation is too slow and would cost more in time and labor.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Standardization:<\/strong> Barcodes and fixed prices help checkout go smoothly, and make prices transparent so shoppers don\u2019t have to haggle.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Thin Margins:<\/strong> Grocery and clothing stores work on volume and low profit margins. They can\u2019t afford to let customers negotiate a few cents on every item, or they\u2019d lose money.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Consistency:<\/strong> Fixed prices mean that every customer is treated the same, which is efficient and keeps shoppers happy (and the store out of legal trouble).<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why Can't ALL Cars Have Barcodes and Set Prices?<\/strong><\/h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Some dealers actually <strong>do<\/strong> use fixed pricing \u2014 this is called \u201cno-haggle\u201d or \u201cone price\u201d selling (CarMax, Tesla). But:<\/p><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Competition:<\/strong> Dealers compete hard and sometimes want to make a deal to win your business, especially on unpopular models or old inventory.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Customer Expectation:<\/strong> Many people feel good \u201cgetting a deal\u201d on a car, so it\u2019s part of the buying culture.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Complex Variables:<\/strong> Cars vary in options, colors, mileage (if used), incentives, etc. Pricing isn\u2019t always as simple as a size Medium blue T-shirt.<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Bottom Line:<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Big purchases<\/strong> like cars = room to negotiate, prices not always displayed.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Everyday goods<\/strong> = fixed prices for speed, fairness, and efficiency.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\"><strong>Want a simpler car buying experience?<\/strong> Look at brands and retailers that advertise \u201cno-haggle\u201d pricing!<\/p><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Let me know if you want tips for getting the best deal on a car!<\/p><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Response A: Great question! The difference comes down to how different markets work and how prici...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p><strong>Response B:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Great question! The difference comes down to how different markets <strong>work<\/strong> and how pricing strategies are designed.<\/p><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>1. Negotiation in Car Sales<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>High Ticket Purchases:<\/strong> Cars are expensive, big decisions. Dealerships know customers spend a lot of time researching and comparing.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Profit Margins:<\/strong> Cars have more room for <strong>markups<\/strong> and discounts than shirts, so sellers can haggle and still make money.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Trade-Ins &amp; Financing:<\/strong> The value of your trade-in car, and the way you finance, gives sellers more ways to adjust the \u201cdeal\u201d, so the final price is often flexible.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Market Practices:<\/strong> Negotiation is a longtime tradition in car sales. Dealers advertise high prices knowing that haggling will happen.<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>2. Fixed Pricing in Low-Cost Retail (e.g., Walmart)<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Low-Cost, High-Volume:<\/strong> Walmart sells millions of shirts. Price negotiation is too slow and would cost more in time and labor.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Standardization:<\/strong> Barcodes and fixed prices help checkout go smoothly, and make prices transparent so shoppers don\u2019t have to haggle.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Thin Margins:<\/strong> Grocery and clothing stores work on volume and low profit margins. They can\u2019t afford to let customers negotiate a few cents on every item, or they\u2019d lose money.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Consistency:<\/strong> Fixed prices mean that every customer is treated the same, which is efficient and keeps shoppers happy (and the store out of legal trouble).<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Why Can't ALL Cars Have Barcodes and Set Prices?<\/strong><\/h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Some dealers actually <strong>do<\/strong> use fixed pricing \u2014 this is called \u201cno-haggle\u201d or \u201cone price\u201d selling (CarMax, Tesla). But:<\/p><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Competition:<\/strong> Dealers compete hard and sometimes want to make a deal to win your business, especially on unpopular models or old inventory.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Customer Expectation:<\/strong> Many people feel good \u201cgetting a deal\u201d on a car, so it\u2019s part of the buying culture.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Complex Variables:<\/strong> Cars vary in options, colors, mileage (if used), incentives, etc. Pricing isn\u2019t always as simple as a size Medium blue T-shirt.<\/li><\/ul><h3 style=\"margin:12px 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Bottom Line:<\/strong><\/h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 12px 24px; padding:0;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Big purchases<\/strong> like cars = room to negotiate, prices not always displayed.<\/li><li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\"><strong>Everyday goods<\/strong> = fixed prices for speed, fairness, and efficiency.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\"><strong>Want a simpler car buying experience?<\/strong> Look at brands and retailers that advertise \u201cno-haggle\u201d pricing!<\/p><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Let me know if you want tips for getting the best deal on a car!<\/p><\/div>","DataExportTag":"P06_V2_ResponseA","QuestionID":"QID233"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID234","SecondaryAttribute":"In the next few questions, rate Response B based on your overall impression, including both its c...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response B based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"In the next few questions, rate Response B based on your overall impression, including both its c...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<strong>In the next few questions, rate Response B based on your overall impression, including both its content and the way it is written. There are no right or wrong answers, we are interested in your honest judgment.<\/strong>","DataExportTag":"P06_Tones_B","QuestionID":"QID234"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID235","SecondaryAttribute":"Did the response address what the user asked for?\u00a01 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<strong>Did the response address what the user asked for?&nbsp;<br><\/strong><em>1 = Not at all, 3 = Partially, 5 = Completely<\/em>","