s) feel condescending, stereotypical, or otherwise socially inappropriate.","DataExportTag":"Q82","QuestionID":"QID82"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID83","SecondaryAttribute":"Prompt","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Prompt 2:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Write a function to find the area of a rectangle.<br>assert python_function(10,20)==200<br>Generate a Python function to solve this problem. Ensure the generated function is named as python_function.<\/p><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel"},"QuestionDescription":"Prompt","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p><strong>Prompt 2:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Write a function to find the area of a rectangle.<br>assert python_function(10,20)==200<br>Generate a Python function to solve this problem. Ensure the generated function is named as python_function.<\/p><\/div>","DataExportTag":"P02","QuestionID":"QID83"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7UHFd5UMl2pr8UK","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID84","SecondaryAttribute":"Response A","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Certainly! Here is the Python function as requested:<\/p><pre style=\"margin:8px 0 12px 0; padding:12px; background:#f6f8fa; border:1px solid #d0d7de; border-radius:6px; white-space:pre-wrap; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><code class=\"language-python\">def python_function(length, width):\n    return length * width<\/code><\/pre><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">You can test it with the assertion:<\/p><pre style=\"margin:8px 0 12px 0; padding:12px; background:#f6f8fa; border:1px solid #d0d7de; border-radius:6px; white-space:pre-wrap; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><code class=\"language-python\">assert python_function(10, 20) == 200<\/code><\/pre><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">This function calculates the area of a rectangle using the formula <strong>area = length \u00d7 width<\/strong>.<\/p><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel"},"QuestionDescription":"Response A","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p><strong>Response A:<\/strong><\/p><div style=\"width:100%; max-width:100%; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Certainly! Here is the Python function as requested:<\/p><pre style=\"margin:8px 0 12px 0; padding:12px; background:#f6f8fa; border:1px solid #d0d7de; border-radius:6px; white-space:pre-wrap; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><code class=\"language-python\">def python_function(length, width):\n    return length * width<\/code><\/pre><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">You can test it with the assertion:<\/p><pre style=\"margin:8px 0 12px 0; padding:12px; background:#f6f8fa; border:1px solid #d0d7de; border-radius:6px; white-space:pre-wrap; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\"><code class=\"language-python\">assert python_function(10, 20) == 200<\/code><\/pre><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">This function calculates the area of a rectangle using the formula <strong>area = length \u00d7 width<\/strong>.<\/p><\/div>","DataExportTag":"P02_V2_ResponseB","QuestionID":"QID84"}},{"Su